{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"automotive-controlled-dassie","creation_channel":"cli","description":"# The gating pip-audit job fails on EVERY Gerrit patchset, blocking all Verified +1 votes\n\n## Symptom\n\n`build-and-test / pip-audit (dependency vulnerabilities)` fails on every patchset run\nobserved today, so no change can reach `Verified +1`. Confirmed across five independent\nruns on different agents' patchsets: 30770494611, 30770603146, 30770604307, 30770971365,\n30771122330, 30771131391. All share head sha 4214516f95 (`origin/main`), and the failures\nare identical, so this is a property of `main`, not of any one change.\n\n## Root cause — a real advisory, NOT a network flake\n\nFrom run 30770494611's job log (the audit step's own output):\n\n    pip-audit attempt 1/3\n    click 8.2.1   PYSEC-2026-2132   8.3.3   Pallets Click, versions 8.3.2 and below,\n      contain a command injection vulnerability in the click.edit() function, allowing\n      attackers to pass arbitrary OS commands from an unprivileged account.\n    ##[error]pip-audit found dependency vulnerabilities (see output). Bump the pinned\n      version, or add --ignore-vuln <ID> with justification if accepted.\n\nIt succeeded on attempt 1 — it REACHED the advisory DB and found a vulnerability. So the\nworkflow's documented infra escape hatch does NOT apply: `_build-and-test.yml`'s failure\npolicy reserves `recheck` for the case where all three attempts fail to reach the DB.\nCommenting `recheck` will not clear this.\n\n`click` is a TRANSITIVE dependency pinned at 8.2.1 in the committed `uv.lock` (line 711);\nit is not pinned in `pyproject.toml`. The advisory appears to have been published after\n`ce5d: go uv-canonical with a committed lock` landed the lock, which is why a previously\ngreen gate went red with no code change.\n\n## Remediation (one of)\n\n1. Refresh the lock so `click` resolves to >= 8.3.3 (the fix version pip-audit names).\n   Preferred: it removes the vulnerability rather than accepting it.\n2. If 8.3.3 is not resolvable under the current constraint set, `--ignore-vuln\n   PYSEC-2026-2132` with a written justification, per the failure policy's explicit\n   provision for that (`_build-and-test.yml`, \"Failure policy\"). Note rebar does not call\n   `click.edit()`, so the exploit path is plausibly not reachable — but that argument\n   belongs IN the justification comment, reviewed, not assumed here.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] `pip-audit` is green on a fresh patchset against `main`\n- [ ] the fix is a lock/pin change or a justified, greppable `--ignore-vuln`, not a\n      blanket skip of the job\n- [ ] if option 2 is taken, the justification names why the vulnerable code path is\n      unreachable from rebar\n\n## Why this is filed separately\n\nDiscovered while landing story 79d5 (DC length convergence), whose diff is two new test\nfiles plus a source comment and touches no dependency pin. A lock refresh is a different\nchange with a different blast radius, and `uv.lock` is outside that story's declared file\nimpact.","id":"e47e-a33d-b9cf-4421","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"pip-audit gate is red on main: click 8.2.1 PYSEC-2026-2132"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1785711581275484001,"uuid":"f73b90a5-3312-4445-b6eb-785c79131655"}